# Set up the environment
Create a folder named "tocopy" on your machine, at /home/$USER/. If you want to use a different name or path, don't forget to adapt the Makefile's "copy" rule's variables.

Prepare a .env file inside.

Example of .env:
````
DOMAIN_NAME=clmmm.42.fr

POSTGRES_USER=insertUSERhere
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=insertPASSWORDhere
POSTGRES_DB=/path/to/your/db
````

CAREFUL: once the username and password have been used to create the database, you won't be able to change them without erasing all its data.

# Make commands
## Build and Launch the stack
To build and launch the stack, type:
```
make
```

## Stop the stack
```
make down
```

## Restart the stack
```
make up
```

## Stop and restart the stack
```
make re
```

## Stop and delete the stack
**!! CAREFUL !!

This action will erase ALL DATA.**

```
make fclean
```

# Secrets management
Secrets are managed by HarshiCorp Vault.

During the building, the stack will inject the environment variables into the Vault docker volume "vault_data". 

It will also generate a certificate, stocked in the docker volume "certs_data", that is shared with NGINX.
